pair Q, P, R, C;

Q = (2.43,3.46);
P = (0,0);
R = (4.43,0);
C = incenter(Q,P,R);

draw(Q--P--R--cycle);
draw(incircle(Q,P,R));
draw(R--C);

label("$Q$", Q, N);
label("$P$", P, SW);
label("$R$", R, SE);
label("$C$", C, N);

[/asy]

Given the function f(x) = (x+3)/(x^2+1), and g(x) = x - ln(x-p).
(I) Find the equation of the tangent line to the graph of f(x) at the point (1/3, f(1/3));
(II) Determine the number of zeros of the function g(x), and explain the reason;
(III) It is known that the sequence {a_n} satisfies: 0 < a_n ≤ 3, n ∈ ℕ*, and 3(a₁ + a₂ + … + a₂₀₁₅) = 2015. If the inequality f(a₁) + f(a₂) + … + f(a₂₀₁₅) ≤ g(x) holds for x ∈ (p, +∞), find the minimum value of the real number p.

In \(\triangle ABC\), the sides opposite to angles \(A\), \(B\), and \(C\) are \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) respectively. It is known that one of the angles equals \(\frac{\pi}{3}\), one of the sides has a length of 8, and the area of the triangle is \(10 \sqrt{3}\).
(I) Determine the value of \(c\);
(II) Determine \(\cos(B-C)\).

According to statistical data, the daily output of a factory does not exceed 200,000 pieces, and the daily defect rate p is approximately related to the daily output x (in 10,000 pieces) by the following relationship:
$$
p= \begin{cases} 
\frac{x^{2}+60}{540} & (0<x\leq 12) \\
\frac{1}{2} & (12<x\leq 20)
\end{cases}
$$
It is known that for each non-defective product produced, a profit of 2 yuan can be made, while producing a defective product results in a loss of 1 yuan. (The factory's daily profit y = daily profit from non-defective products - daily loss from defective products).
(1) Express the daily profit y (in 10,000 yuan) as a function of the daily output x (in 10,000 pieces);
(2) At what daily output (in 10,000 pieces) is the daily profit maximized? What is the maximum daily profit in yuan?

