Read the following material: Expressing a fraction as the sum of two fractions is called expressing the fraction as "partial fractions." Example: Express the fraction  (1-3x)/(x^2-1)  as partial fractions. Solution: Let (1-3x)/(x^2-1)=M/(x+1)+N/(x-1), cross multiply on the right side of the equation, we get (M(x-1)+N(x+1))/( (x+1)(x-1) ) = ((M+N)x+(N-M))/(x^2-1). According to the question, we have { M+N=3, N-M=1 }, solving this system gives {M=-2, N=-1}, so (1-3x)/(x^2-1)= -2/(x+1)-1/(x-1). Please use the method learned above to solve the following problems:
(1) Express the fraction (2n+1)/(n^2+n) as partial fractions;
(2) Following the pattern in (1), find the value of 3/(1×2)-5/(2×3)+7/(3×4)-9/(4×5)+⋯+39/(19×20)-41/(20×21).

