(I) Find the magnitude of the angle between \(\overrightarrow{a}\) and \(\overrightarrow{b}\);

(II) Find the value of \(|3\overrightarrow{a} + \overrightarrow{b}|\).

Cube $ABCDEFGH,$ labeled as shown below, has edge length $1$ and is cut by a plane passing through vertex $D$ and the midpoints $M$ and $N$ of $\overline{AB}$ and $\overline{CG}$ respectively. The plane divides the cube into two solids.  Find the volume of the larger of the two solids.

[asy]
import cse5;
unitsize(8mm);
pathpen=black;
pair A = (0,0), B = (3.8,0), C = (5.876,1.564), D = (2.076,1.564), E = (0,3.8), F = (3.8,3.8), G = (5.876,5.364), H = (2.076,5.364), M = (1.9,0), N = (5.876,3.465);
pair[] dotted = {A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,M,N};
D(A--B--C--G--H--E--A);
D(E--F--B);
D(F--G);
pathpen=dashed;
D(A--D--H);
D(D--C);
dot(dotted);
label("$A$",A,SW);
label("$B$",B,S);
label("$C$",C,SE);
label("$D$",D,NW);
label("$E$",E,W);
label("$F$",F,SE);
label("$G$",G,NE);
label("$H$",H,NW);
label("$M$",M,S);
label("$N$",N,NE);
[/asy]

Consider three numbers \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) associated with three angles \(A\), \(B\), and \(C\), respectively, where no relationship among the angles is assumed. It is given that \(\cos C = \frac{5}{13}\) and \(\cos(A - B) = \frac{3}{5}\). 

